-- A known annotation that does not have the form it needs is ignored with a
-- warning, as an unknown one is, and does not end the lexer. Three ways to get
-- @lang wrong: nothing after it, a tab where the space goes (line 6), and a
-- language code that is not ASCII.
@lang
@lang	en
@lang é
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `add one` n IS n + 1

#ASSERT (`add one` 1) EQUALS 2
